nodecode-recall-vault is a rewrite of tydavid5's tydavid5/recall-vault:

  https://github.com/tydavid5/recall-vault
  commit e564eb53143840540d1987b48906e1602050c73f
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Taiwo John (tydavid5) (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the policy engine (per-transaction cap, daily cap, confirm
threshold, allowlist, the ALLOWED / BLOCKED / NEEDS_CONFIRMATION decision and
its order), the two JSON files under the plugin data directory, the five
tools and their JSON answers, the audit ledger and its 200-entry cap, the
spent-today reset, the remembered rules, and the /recall-vault command.

Left out, and why: the Hermes hook names. The original hooked pre_tool_call,
post_tool_call and pre_llm_call; this image has one around-chain over every
tool dispatch, so the payment gate and the audit booking are one function on
the :TOOL point, and there is no post_tool_call to keep in step — the
approval answer and the call's own result are read where the call runs.
The per-turn reminder rides a standing harness section rather than a
pre_llm_call hook, so it survives a folded or compacted conversation without
detecting one. The Hermes approval prompt became this image's operator
question (Allow once / Deny), which is the same gate with the surface's own
card. The plugin's own tool names, argument names, JSON members and
/recall-vault subcommands are unchanged, so anything written against the
original reads the same here.
